insert into public.courses values ('geometry','{"id":"geometry","title":"Geometry","subject":"Geometry","grades":[6,10],"description":"Explore introductory geometry lessons.","units":[{"id":"g6-volume","title":"Space inside a box","grades":[6],"lessons":[{"id":"g6-box-volume","title":"Volume of a rectangular prism","explanation":"Volume measures the space inside a solid. A rectangular prism has volume length × width × height. Use cubic units, such as cubic centimeters.","example":"A box 4 cm long, 3 cm wide and 2 cm high holds 4 × 3 × 2 = 24 cubic centimeters. Its 12-square-centimeter base has two layers.","questions":[{"id":"g6-box-volume-q1","prompt":"A rectangular box is 5 cm long, 2 cm wide and 3 cm high. What is its volume in cubic centimeters?","answer":"30","hint":"Find the base area, then multiply by the height.","explanation":"5 × 2 = 10 square centimeters per layer. 10 × 3 = 30 cubic centimeters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"easy"},{"id":"g6-box-volume-q2","prompt":"A rectangular prism is 1.5 m long, 2 m wide and 4 m high. What is its volume in cubic meters?","answer":"12","hint":"Decimal side lengths use the same rule: multiply all three dimensions.","explanation":"1.5 × 2 × 4 = 3 × 4 = 12 cubic meters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"g6-box-volume-q3","prompt":"A rectangular box has volume 48 cubic centimeters, length 4 cm and width 3 cm. What is its height in centimeters?","answer":"4","hint":"The base area is 4 × 3. Divide the volume by that area.","explanation":"48 ÷ (4 × 3) = 48 ÷ 12 = 4 centimeters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"medium"}]}],"requires":[],"x":0,"y":0},{"id":"triangle-angles","title":"Angles in triangles","grades":[10],"requires":[],"x":260,"y":0,"lessons":[{"id":"triangle-angles-practice","title":"Angles in triangles","explanation":"The three interior angles of a triangle add to 180 degrees.","example":"If two angles are 50° and 60°, the third is 180 − 110 = 70°.","questions":[{"id":"triangle-angles-q1","prompt":"A triangle has angles of 45° and 65°. Find the third angle in degrees.","answer":"70","hint":"The three interior angles of a triangle add to 180 degrees.","explanation":"180 − 45 − 65 = 70 degrees.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"easy"},{"id":"triangle-angles-q2","prompt":"A right triangle has one acute angle of 32°. Find its other acute angle in degrees.","answer":"58","hint":"The three interior angles of a triangle add to 180 degrees.","explanation":"180 − 90 − 32 = 58 degrees.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"easy"}]}]},{"id":"triangle-area","title":"Area of triangles","grades":[10],"requires":["triangle-angles"],"x":520,"y":0,"lessons":[{"id":"triangle-area-practice","title":"Area of triangles","explanation":"The area of a triangle is one half of base times perpendicular height.","example":"Base 8 and height 5 gives area 8 × 5 ÷ 2 = 20.","questions":[{"id":"triangle-area-q1","prompt":"A triangle has base 12 cm and perpendicular height 7 cm. Find its area in square centimeters.","answer":"42","hint":"The area of a triangle is one half of base times perpendicular height.","explanation":"12 × 7 ÷ 2 = 42 square centimeters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"easy"},{"id":"triangle-area-q2","prompt":"A triangle has area 30 square units and base 10 units. Find its perpendicular height.","answer":"6","hint":"The area of a triangle is one half of base times perpendicular height.","explanation":"30 = 10 × h ÷ 2, so h = 6.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"easy"}]}]},{"id":"path-g6-triangle-measure","title":"Finding triangle area","grades":[6],"requires":[],"lessons":[{"id":"g6-triangle-measure","title":"Finding triangle area","explanation":"A triangle is half a rectangle with the same base and perpendicular height. Its area is base × height ÷ 2.","example":"A triangle with base 6 cm and perpendicular height 4 cm has area 6 × 4 ÷ 2 = 12 square centimeters.","questions":[{"id":"g6-triangle-measure-q1","prompt":"A triangle has base 8 cm and perpendicular height 3 cm. What is its area in square centimeters?","answer":"12","hint":"Multiply the base and height, then halve the result.","explanation":"8 × 3 ÷ 2 = 12 square centimeters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"easy"},{"id":"g6-triangle-measure-q2","prompt":"A triangle has base 5 m and perpendicular height 6 m. What is its area in square meters?","answer":"15","hint":"A matching rectangle has area 5 × 6.","explanation":"5 × 6 ÷ 2 = 15 square meters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"g6-triangle-measure-q3","prompt":"A triangle has area 24 square centimeters and base 8 cm. What is its perpendicular height in centimeters?","answer":"6","hint":"Double the area, then divide by the base.","explanation":"2 × 24 ÷ 8 = 6 centimeters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"medium"}]}],"x":0,"y":200},{"id":"path-g10-pythagoras","title":"The Pythagorean theorem","grades":[10],"requires":[],"lessons":[{"id":"g10-pythagoras","title":"The Pythagorean theorem","explanation":"For a right triangle, a² + b² = c², where c is the hypotenuse opposite the right angle.","example":"Legs 3 and 4 give c² = 9 + 16 = 25, so c = 5.","questions":[{"id":"g10-pythagoras-q1","prompt":"A right triangle has legs 6 cm and 8 cm. What is its hypotenuse in centimeters?","answer":"10","hint":"Square each leg, add, then take the positive square root.","explanation":"6² + 8² = 100, so c = 10 centimeters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"easy"},{"id":"g10-pythagoras-q2","prompt":"A right triangle has hypotenuse 13 m and one leg 5 m. What is its other leg in meters?","answer":"12","hint":"Subtract 5² from 13², then take the positive square root.","explanation":"169 − 25 = 144, so the other leg is 12 meters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"g10-pythagoras-q3","prompt":"A square has side length 5 units. What is the square of its diagonal length?","answer":"50","hint":"The diagonal makes a right triangle with two legs of length 5.","explanation":"d² = 5² + 5² = 50.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"medium"}]}],"x":260,"y":200},{"id":"path-g10-circles","title":"Area and circumference of circles","grades":[10],"requires":["path-g10-pythagoras"],"lessons":[{"id":"g10-circles","title":"Area and circumference of circles","explanation":"For radius r, area = πr² and circumference = 2πr. The diameter is twice the radius. Use π = 3.14 in this lesson.","example":"A circle with radius 2 has area 3.14 × 2² = 12.56 square units.","questions":[{"id":"g10-circles-q1","prompt":"Using π = 3.14, find the area of a circle with radius 3 cm, in square centimeters.","answer":"28.26","hint":"Square the radius, then multiply by 3.14.","explanation":"3.14 × 3² = 3.14 × 9 = 28.26.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"easy"},{"id":"g10-circles-q2","prompt":"Using π = 3.14, find the circumference of a circle with radius 5 m, in meters.","answer":"31.4","hint":"Multiply 2 × 3.14 × 5.","explanation":"The circumference is 31.4 meters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"g10-circles-q3","prompt":"Using π = 3.14, find the area of a circle with diameter 8 cm, in square centimeters.","answer":"50.24","hint":"First halve the diameter to get the radius.","explanation":"r = 4. Area = 3.14 × 4² = 50.24 square centimeters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"medium"}]}],"x":520,"y":200}],"planned":false}') on conflict(id) do update set content=excluded.content;
insert into public.units values ('g6-volume','geometry','{"id":"g6-volume","title":"Space inside a box","grades":[6],"lessons":[{"id":"g6-box-volume","title":"Volume of a rectangular prism","explanation":"Volume measures the space inside a solid. A rectangular prism has volume length × width × height. Use cubic units, such as cubic centimeters.","example":"A box 4 cm long, 3 cm wide and 2 cm high holds 4 × 3 × 2 = 24 cubic centimeters. Its 12-square-centimeter base has two layers.","questions":[{"id":"g6-box-volume-q1","prompt":"A rectangular box is 5 cm long, 2 cm wide and 3 cm high. What is its volume in cubic centimeters?","answer":"30","hint":"Find the base area, then multiply by the height.","explanation":"5 × 2 = 10 square centimeters per layer. 10 × 3 = 30 cubic centimeters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"easy"},{"id":"g6-box-volume-q2","prompt":"A rectangular prism is 1.5 m long, 2 m wide and 4 m high. What is its volume in cubic meters?","answer":"12","hint":"Decimal side lengths use the same rule: multiply all three dimensions.","explanation":"1.5 × 2 × 4 = 3 × 4 = 12 cubic meters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"medium"},{"id":"g6-box-volume-q3","prompt":"A rectangular box has volume 48 cubic centimeters, length 4 cm and width 3 cm. What is its height in centimeters?","answer":"4","hint":"The base area is 4 × 3. Divide the volume by that area.","explanation":"48 ÷ (4 × 3) = 48 ÷ 12 = 4 centimeters.","kind":"numeric","difficulty":"medium"}]}],"requires":[],"x":0,"y":0}') on conflict(id) do update set content=excluded.content;
